{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony","id":918739,"title":"Silver Weapons and Harmony","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-21T12:19:15-07:00","id":918739,"title":"Silver Weapons and Harmony","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> I realize this may be a stupid question, but according to the way Harmony Sins work, if you're packing Silver weapons as a Werewolf, that means you have to do a check on your Harmony, right? Well, does that count for every single weapon and bullet, meaning that you have to make a check for every bullet that you have or acquire or, in my case, hand-load? And if you don't use it, you just stockpile it, how often do you make a roll?<br /> <br /> I mean, say you're playing in a Lone Wolf chronicle, using the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide for Lone Wolves, and you acquire 200lbs. of Silver that you want to use to hand-load your own .50 Cal BMG rounds for you M82A1 Barrett Anti-Material Rifle? How often should you have to make a Harmony Check for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:33:14-07:00","id":918744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wayfinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony#post918739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">according to the way Harmony Sins work, if you're packing Silver weapons as a Werewolf, that means you have to do a check on your Harmony, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of your mention of the Chronicler's Guide and the Harmony sin I'm guessing you're using first edition. In first edition, only if you're at Harmony 9 or 10. Otherwise the Harmony Breaking Point is done for 'using a silver weapon against another werewolf.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, does that count for every single weapon and bullet, meaning that you have to make a check for every bullet that you have or acquire or, in my case, hand-load? And if you don't use it, you just stockpile it, how often do you make a roll? </div> </div> </div>The Harmony 9 sin is for 'carrying a silver weapon.' I would throw in an intent to use it as a qualifier, even if it's using it in the far future, as opposed to picking up a silver weapon someone else was using and carrying it to a furnace to melt it down. But you might add modifiers in the form of penalties for an abundance of silver weaponry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, say you're playing in a Lone Wolf chronicle, using the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide for Lone Wolves, and you acquire 200lbs. of Silver that you want to use to hand-load your own .50 Cal BMG rounds for you M82A1 Barrett Anti-Material Rifle? How often should you have to make a Harmony Check for that? </div> </div> </div>I'd consider the rifle the silver weapon, not the individual bullets. Each fight where you used it would probably demand a Harmony check for using a silver weapon, while just carrying it around with intent to use would be a Harmony check every scene or so.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, in second edition, the Harmony sin is solely for, 'using a silver weapon against another werewolf.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:44:46-07:00","id":918750,"title":"","content":"Well, we're trying to integrate the rules into 2E. I don't personally have the 2E book yet, and my ST is trying to run a 2E game for another group of players who have called upon my character for help in killing off a bunch of Pure. I figured using the weapon in a fight would call for a Harmony Check, but we just didn't know for certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T13:12:09-07:00","id":919284,"title":"","content":"Using a Silver Weapon against another werewolf is a breaking point towards flesh in 2.0. No matter your harmony level.<br /> <br /> Then there's always The People Do Not Murder the People to think about. Silver is not a non-lethal solution. So it depends on the stance you and other nearby Uratha in the setting take on the Pure counting regarding that law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T15:00:43-07:00","id":919963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrimsonOwl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=919284#post919284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using a Silver Weapon against another werewolf is a breaking point towards flesh in 2.0. No matter your harmony level.<br /> <br /> Then there's always The People Do Not Murder the People to think about. Silver is not a non-lethal solution. So it depends on the stance you and other nearby Uratha in the setting take on the Pure counting regarding that law.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Lone Wolf Chronicle I'm in is a bit of a quandary in that regard. We've been struggling with the 1E version of Harmony within the new hacks applied by the Lone Wolf rules from the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide, and I've finally got a good run-down of the 2E approach (Uratha can now mate with other Uratha?). The story is that Max, the Lone Wolf, doesn't really regard himself as a Forsaken or a Pure. While we've gone along that he's a Ghost Wolf, he doesn't even consider himself a member of any tribe, or any lodge, much less any pack at all. Over the course of the past year and a half of playing, he's developed a rather potent Totem that the ST uses to keep him relatively sane. He sees all the supernatural, to include himself, as threats to the humans he's trying to protect from them, and as such he's wiped out whole packs of Werewolves (all of them Pure) in the past for their transgressions into his territory, hence keeping stockpiles of silver ready to go (one of my better applications was loading silver slugs into shotgun rounds for his AA-12 automatic shotgun, which was before he got his hands on a Barrett). <br /> <br /> In spite of the power of the Totem, the main struggle he's had was keeping sane, balancing the Werewolf nature with his human nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T17:16:22-07:00","id":920018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wayfinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=919963#post919963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uratha can now mate with other Uratha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While we've gone along that he's a Ghost Wolf, he doesn't even consider himself a member of any tribe </div> </div> </div>That is a Ghost Wolf. Well, if he hasn't joined one, at least. Werewolves are 'born' Forsaken, on the Luna side of things. They only become Pure if they have their renown brands burned off of them. So technically you can be a Ghost Wolf Forsaken who hunts down other Forsaken, kills Lunes and is trying to figure out a way to blow up the moon. It's one of the reasons Ghost Wolves aren't easily trusted.<br /> <br /> Presumably alternative methods of Harmony will pop up, including some customization options, if we continue to get books. One of the other differences between Harmony in first and second edition is that you do not become a zi'ir and lose your character at low Ranks, you just find it harder to live with other humans. Harmony is not human versus werewolf, it's flesh versus spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-23-2016, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T18:15:09-07:00","id":920045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=920018#post920018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is a Ghost Wolf. Well, if he hasn't joined one, at least. Werewolves are 'born' Forsaken, on the Luna side of things. They only become Pure if they have their renown brands burned off of them. So technically you can be a Ghost Wolf Forsaken who hunts down other Forsaken, kills Lunes and is trying to figure out a way to blow up the moon. It's one of the reasons Ghost Wolves aren't easily trusted.<br /> <br /> Presumably alternative methods of Harmony will pop up, including some customization options, if we continue to get books. One of the other differences between Harmony in first and second edition is that you do not become a zi'ir and lose your character at low Ranks, you just find it harder to live with other humans. Harmony is not human versus werewolf, it's flesh versus spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we've been running this chronicle as though the whole mythos of the Forsaken and Pure are complete scams, from Max's perspective. Not necessarily false, and maybe Max is wrong, but he could also be more right than even he knows. It's a minor aspect of the chronicle compared to the Action/Superhero theme going, and we're a bit more oriented on putting the combat rules through its paces, and seeing just what a Werewolf really can do, physically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T18:17:36-07:00","id":920047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=920018#post920018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is a Ghost Wolf. Well, if he hasn't joined one, at least. Werewolves are 'born' Forsaken, on the Luna side of things. They only become Pure if they have their renown brands burned off of them. So technically you can be a Ghost Wolf Forsaken who hunts down other Forsaken, kills Lunes and is trying to figure out a way to blow up the moon. It's one of the reasons Ghost Wolves aren't easily trusted.<br /> <br /> Presumably alternative methods of Harmony will pop up, including some customization options, if we continue to get books. One of the other differences between Harmony in first and second edition is that you do not become a zi'ir and lose your character at low Ranks, you just find it harder to live with other humans. Harmony is not human versus werewolf, it's flesh versus spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Forsaken is specifically a member of one of the forsaken tribes, there's no such thing as a forsaken ghost wolf. By default it's 'born' ghost wolf and then they can become forsaken or pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T18:28:09-07:00","id":920058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=920047#post920047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forsaken is specifically a member of one of the forsaken tribes</div> </div> </div> </div>In-world, according to the Pure. But anything that isn't Pure has the Forsaken template, which includes the Ghost Wolves. And the Pure don't likely care if you're a member of a tribe or not, as long as you have an Auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T20:08:41-07:00","id":920107,"title":"","content":"Silver weapons deal aggravated damage to werewolves, and cause a Breaking Point towards flesh. Eating human or wolf flesh for Essence deals aggravated damage and causes a Breaking Point towards spirit. It should be very easy for this character to maintain balanced Harmony. If it's below 5, use silver weapons. If it's above 5, use bite attacks and swallow. Have fun being reviled by Pure and Forsaken as a kinslayer and a cannibal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:58:23-07:00","id":920189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=920107#post920107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver weapons deal aggravated damage to werewolves, and cause a Breaking Point towards flesh. Eating human or wolf flesh for Essence deals aggravated damage and causes a Breaking Point towards spirit. It should be very easy for this character to maintain balanced Harmony. If it's below 5, use silver weapons. If it's above 5, use bite attacks and swallow. Have fun being reviled by Pure and Forsaken as a kinslayer and a cannibal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, does biting count as eating? Because Max hasn't eaten either a human or a werewolf yet. He's bitten them, but usually ends up washing his mouth out in Listerine. Eating a werewolf is like eating a dog. Would you eat a dog? And, eating a human, no matter how delicious and tempting it might be, is still eating a human being. He'd accept kinslayer if it scares folks. Terror is a good weapon. So if there's a way to maintain balance without resorting to cannibalism, I'd appreciate it. <br /> <br /> I figure in keeping with the spirit of the Lone Wolf rules, participating or leading the Siskur-Dah is a no-no, and there ought not to be any sin against killing a packmate, since he doesn't have a pack. And spending more than two days with other werewolves is also a no-no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T23:14:39-07:00","id":920199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wayfinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=920189#post920189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, does biting count as eating? Because Max hasn't eaten either a human or a werewolf yet. He's bitten them, but usually ends up washing his mouth out in Listerine. Eating a werewolf is like eating a dog. Would you eat a dog? And, eating a human, no matter how delicious and tempting it might be, is still eating a human being. He'd accept kinslayer if it scares folks. Terror is a good weapon. So if there's a way to maintain balance without resorting to cannibalism, I'd appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you've got to actually swallow something to eat it. Your character has an... unusual mix of moral compunctions if he's cool with mass murder and has aspirations of genocide but draws the line at eating dog meat. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wayfinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=920189#post920189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure in keeping with the spirit of the Lone Wolf rules, participating or leading the Siskur-Dah is a no-no, and there ought not to be any sin against killing a packmate, since he doesn't have a pack. And spending more than two days with other werewolves is also a no-no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... He could spend a few months in the spirit world, I guess? Or get a flesh Touchstone and then kill them. I've got to be honest, I don't understand this character's motivations at all, so sorry if any of my suggestions are against his code or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T23:32:25-07:00","id":920208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No, you've got to actually swallow something to eat it. Your character has an... unusual mix of moral compunctions if he's cool with mass murder and has aspirations of genocide but draws the line at eating dog meat. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I'm approaching this character from the perspective of someone who's been turned into a monster by a fiend who attempted to bring him into his little satanic frat party, wanting to call people with some sort of special rite to eat them (or worse, from what I gathered). After a little spat where he ended up decapitating the mentor with a train and killing the rest of the pack, Max has sought to either find a cure (which there isn't any) or control the beast within, and use it to fight against other monsters and baddies. So he doesn't know the Oath of the Moon, because he never took it. He doesn't know the rules. He sees those that have strangely embraced their Werewolf side as psychotic and downright evil, thinking that it's kind of bad to hunt down innocent people. Just because it might be natural doesn't make it right. It's like you've just been made aware of a bunch of aliens who have secretly declared war on the human race, and the human race wasn't told. What would you do?<br /> <br /> Now, he hasn't killed a Forsaken yet, and only recently has he learned the difference. It's a small distinction, but at least the Forsaken that he's met have respected his territory. For now. Of course, a good Intimidation skill score helped in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T05:27:16-07:00","id":920298,"title":"","content":"There's a sample Ghost Wolf like this in the second edition book, it's not a healthy way to do things. In second edition, at least. Rejecting your spirit side leads to high Harmony, which makes you more susceptible to death rage, with more triggers, and makes it harder to shape-shift and impossible to Reach.<br /> <br /> In either edition he would be ripe for slavery by some powerful spirit or another. That sort of self-hatred coupled with psychopathic murder streaks isn't good for the mental defenses.<br /> <br /> With the eating, it comes up because if you bite someone to eat you do Aggravated damage. If you just bite them to bite them, you do Lethal. The former requires you to eat to do that extra damage, and gain Essence for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-24-2016, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T10:25:33-07:00","id":920442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wayfinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=920208#post920208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm approaching this character from the perspective of someone who's been turned into a monster by a fiend who attempted to bring him into his little satanic frat party, wanting to call people with some sort of special rite to eat them (or worse, from what I gathered). After a little spat where he ended up decapitating the mentor with a train and killing the rest of the pack, Max has sought to either find a cure (which there isn't any) or control the beast within, and use it to fight against other monsters and baddies. So he doesn't know the Oath of the Moon, because he never took it. He doesn't know the rules. He sees those that have strangely embraced their Werewolf side as psychotic and downright evil, thinking that it's kind of bad to hunt down innocent people. Just because it might be natural doesn't make it right. It's like you've just been made aware of a bunch of aliens who have secretly declared war on the human race, and the human race wasn't told. What would you do?<br /> <br /> Now, he hasn't killed a Forsaken yet, and only recently has he learned the difference. It's a small distinction, but at least the Forsaken that he's met have respected his territory. For now. Of course, a good Intimidation skill score helped in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Yeah, this character <i>should</i> have very high Harmony, then. That's the intent of the 2e Harmony system, if you don't embrace your spirit nature and your hunter's instincts, you're going to have a hard time shape shifting, and Death Rage is going to hit you often and hard. That's fine, that's a valid character choice. I love high Harmony characters.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Essentially, Max is well set-up for a nice little character arc where he rejects his werewolf nature at first and looks for a cure, finds that there is no cure so he tries to learn to control it, ends up doing a lot of damage to himself and others in the process, and eventually figures out that the only way to control it is - ironically enough - to embrace it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-24-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T21:39:09-07:00","id":920778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ah. Yeah, this character </span></span></span><i>should</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> have very high Harmony, then. That's the intent of the 2e Harmony system, if you don't embrace your spirit nature and your hunter's instincts, you're going to have a hard time shape shifting, and Death Rage is going to hit you often and hard. That's fine, that's a valid character choice. I love high Harmony characters.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">EDIT: Essentially, Max is well set-up for a nice little character arc where he rejects his werewolf nature at first and looks for a cure, finds that there is no cure so he tries to learn to control it, ends up doing a lot of damage to himself and others in the process, and eventually figures out that the only way to control it is - ironically enough - to embrace it.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>There were some things I left out because I don't want to be too controversial. But, yes, he has a hard time shape-shifting, and he's practically been mugged repeatedly by Death Rage. Getting to Portland was all about finding some sort of cure, all the while fighting off baddies, and finding out if a werewolf could go toe-to-toe with a Kodiak Grizzly Bear (the answer is yes, but it was a close fight). We emphasized the combat aspect of the game more mainly, and only recently, since abandoning the pursuit of a cure, have we begun exploring the conflicting nature of the human and the werewolf side. Max doesn't have many human friends; even the two allies he has don't really like being around him because he's a bit like Ash from Evil Dead and Deadpool, albeit a bit more moral. <br /> <br /> The ST has been gracious, though, with the Totem. The Totem helps him to control the Werewolf within, but he's got a huge list of bans, which he repeatedly violates (except when he's killing vampires - he can kill as many as he wants), and then he atones for it. He goes hunting a lot, and he likes it. He hasn't gone up against too many of the spirits out there, like the Hosts and such, but that's mainly because I think my ST doesn't quite know how to integrate them into the chronicle, but he's going to try integrating them in the new Boondock Wolves (like the Boondock Saints) chronicle we're playing now, where Max is asked for help by a bunch of young Forsaken werewolves to fight a bunch of Pure. (By the way, his concept was that he was a former US Army Ranger that was &quot;peered&quot; out, due to his then unknown werewolf nature, and ended up in the French Foreign Legion where he experienced First Change.)<br /> <br /> Integrating Max into the new chronicle has been fun so far. We don't know if he will end up joining them (not likely, due to the Lone Wolf stuff) or they end up joining him. It'll be interesting to see how it plays out. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T09:18:34-07:00","id":921519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=920107#post920107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver weapons deal aggravated damage to werewolves, and cause a Breaking Point towards flesh. Eating human or wolf flesh for Essence deals aggravated damage and causes a Breaking Point towards spirit. It should be very easy for this character to maintain balanced Harmony. If it's below 5, use silver weapons. If it's above 5, use bite attacks and swallow. Have fun being reviled by Pure and Forsaken as a kinslayer and a cannibal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book specifically states that about Human and Wolf, but I don't remember reading about eating Werewolf Flesh. The original poster seems to think that eating Werewolf Flesh will also cause aggravated damage, is he right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T09:57:57-07:00","id":921531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=921519#post921519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book specifically states that about Human and Wolf, but I don't remember reading about eating Werewolf Flesh. The original poster seems to think that eating Werewolf Flesh will also cause aggravated damage, is he right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. By 'wolf' it means werewolf. It comes up in a later section under Cannibalism or something as well. It's been confirmed by the writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:17:39-07:00","id":922268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In either edition he would be ripe for slavery by some powerful spirit or another. That sort of self-hatred coupled with psychopathic murder streaks isn't good for the mental defenses.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. That's precisely what we've done. So what's the most powerful spirit there is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:40:31-07:00","id":922284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wayfinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=922268#post922268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the most powerful spirit there is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Known, there's Luna and Helios. There's probably other outer space ones that aren't able to act on Earth because of Luna. But there's trillions of spirits and probably hundreds of thousands that are beyond the reach of mortals and werewolves, who cannot even fit into the world without threatening to destroy it like Fenris-Ur.<br /> <br /> More likely a werewolf would be enslaved by a powerful spirit in your territory, which would depend entirely on your territory. Another might wander through. It wouldn't really have to be a powerful spirit, either, considering his knowledge of the Hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T17:57:35-07:00","id":923596,"title":"","content":"On a related topic, normally the Pure do not seem to use silver weapons, but could an Ivory Claw instruct his human minions to hunt forsaken with silver weapons? Would that violate any oaths or be technically valid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:27:09-07:00","id":923610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918739-silver-weapons-and-harmony?p=923596#post923596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related topic, normally the Pure do not seem to use silver weapons, but could an Ivory Claw instruct his human minions to hunt forsaken with silver weapons? Would that violate any oaths or be technically valid?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do use them, just very carefully. An Ivory Claw could do that, but I wouldn't see them trusting a human with silver when it does more damage to the Ivory Claw and humans can go Berserk and start attacking their former masters.<br /> <br /> Technically using silver isn't part of any Oath. I imagine it to be a Breaking Point away from spirit because it's not very spirit-like to use your own Bane. Though Predator Kings do have an oath against things made by mankind, you could get around it by forging the weapon yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}